      "budget_share": 0.6,
      "why": "unrolled_k is the critical family for the system constraint: sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5 us means all 32 burst results must return within 0.5 us of the tick. With a 1 us tick period, the CORDIC has at most 0.5 us to drain 32 requests. iterative takes N+3 cycles per result (e.g. 15+3=18 cycles), so 32 results need 32*18=576 cycles — far too slow unless Fmax is very high. unrolled_k with k=2-4 reduces cycles/result to ceil(N/k)+3 (e.g. N=14, k=4 -> 4+3=7 cycles), so 32 results need 32*7=224 cycles. At a plausible Fmax of ~100-200 MHz, 224 cycles = 1.1-2.2 us, still tight; k=4 with lower N or higher Fmax may just meet 0.5 us. The throughput_msps >= 32 constraint also pushes toward higher k. k is capped at 4 because k=5-8 adds significant area (wider combinational logic per stage) and the area objective penalises that; the trade-off between k (speed) and area is the main axis to explore here. data_width/n_iter/guards mirror iterative to keep accuracy >= 12 bits at minimal width."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec has three hard constraints: throughput_msps >= 32, max_abs_err <= 2^-12, and sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5 us. The system constraint is the binding one: a 32-request burst every 1 us must fully drain within 0.5 us. This rules out slow iterative designs unless Fmax is extremely high, and pushes toward unrolled_k with moderate k. The area objective means we want the smallest data_width and n_iter that still give accuracy_bits >= 12, which is roughly data_width 14-16 and n_iter 12-16. I split the budget 40/60 between iterative and unrolled_k: iterative anchors the min-area corner of the Pareto front (it will be the cheapest design if it can meet the system constraint at high Fmax), while unrolled_k is where the feasible region for the batch-latency constraint actually lives. Rounding is included in both because it is free accuracy. I keep angle_guard and frac_guard low (0-2) to minimise area; if accuracy is insufficient, the next round can widen them. k is limited to 2-4 to avoid the area blow-up of high-k unrolling while still exploring the speed/area trade-off that determines whether the 0.5 us batch constraint is met."
}

